A||N||3||Seanh||Any harm in changing oil brands???||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||01-20-2001||08:15 PM||||I was just asking this because of my dad. He is no where near a do-it-yourself mechanic, in fact Iv probally forgotten more then he'll ever know about cars. But, he keeps telling me 1)it is very harmful to your car to switch oil brands(like Castrol to Mobil 1) and 2)That synthetic's are a rip off, and he hears you should only use the 50/50 part synthetic blends, and 3)Synthetic is harmful to your engine if you've never used it before. In my mind, this a lot of crap. How could changing oil brands be bad for the engine, unless you switch to a bad brand? Is there any harm in changing oil brands, or changing to synthetic? My argument is that synthetic's dont break down as quickly as regular oil does, therefore it is extra protection if you miss an oil change deadline. I dont know it all, but I thought synthetic was good, especially for high milage engines. Corect me if I'm wrong.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto (3.4 Conversion in Progress)<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||01-20-2001||09:23 PM||||There was n interesting editorial in Car and Driver in the past year about this subject. I'll look through my back issues for the date.<BR>Basically, I can't see any harm in switching brands.  As far as the "Synthetic Oil rip-off" there are some synthetics that are using poorer quality base. My feeling is that Mobil One started the dance, and that's who I am sticking with. As synthetics become more popular, no doubt other manufacturers will introduce products that technically can wear the synthetic name, but are of inferior grade.<BR>As far as putting synth into a hig mileage engine, I have heard anecdotes about it loosening gunk that is preventing leaks. I think a bigger danger is using that low-viscosity 5-30w synth oil in an engine that is getting a bit loose in the tolerances. <BR>   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||01-20-2001||10:12 PM||||I was wondering about it causing leaks like that. This particular car I am wanting to change the oil in has a nasty rear-main bearing seal leak. I put in some bearin' seal leak stopper, but it hasnt seemed to help much. I am going to keep useing it at every oil change. I should replace the seals, but I dont feel up to it this winter. You guys think I should switch from (non-synthetic)Valvoline to Mobile One Synthetic for this engine. Actually the leaking engine is in our '90 Lincoln TC, it only has 108K miles on it. My Fiero has 118K on it, and has no leaks, think it should be switched to full synthetic?||||reg||1
Z||000003||ur2biteme||01-21-2001||01:28 AM||||allright, someone correct me if i'm wrong here, but i would stay with conventional oils in the engine that is allready leaking.  reason why, (this is the part i want corrected) from what i have come to understand, synthetics tend to be more likely to slip past seals that may or may not be leaking now and make exhisting leaks worse.  i wouldnt think it would make the engine run worse, but you'll be replacing lost oil at a much more noticable rate, both in quarts and in dollars.<P>now, for the engine that isnt leaking, i dont see any harm in trying it at least once, but dont be supprised if it starts leaking after a couple hundred miles from the oil change for the same reason mentioned earlier.  <P>my car likes to mark it's territory well (healthy oil leak) so i avoid the synthetics.  i use the conventional Quaker State (not sure which line, but the one that states that it protects for over 3000 miles) mainly because it looked the cleanest coming out of the bottle, and i noticed my car ran much smoother and quieter with that in it.  <P>once again, correct me if i'm wrong, but i hope i helped.<P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>170k awaiting a tranny:(<BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme</A> ||||reg||1
